=== PE 905: Inclusion-Exclusion Analysis ===

f(b, k) counts k-digit base-b strings that are pandigital

Structure:
  Total k-digit strings (nonzero first): (b-1)·b^{k-1}
  For s excluded digits, contribution:
    (-1)^s · C(choose which digits to exclude) · (b-s)^{k-1} · choices
  where 'choices' = (b-s-1) if 0 is kept, (b-s) if 0 is excluded

The inclusion-exclusion accounts for the constraint that
every digit 0..b-1 must appear at least once.

For small b, f(b,k) grows as b!·S(k,b) where S(k,b) are
Stirling numbers of the second kind, counting surjections.
